  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">23M-EADEN - Waste Management for Safe Environment and Climate Resilient Livelihoods in Uganda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Today&#x2019;s scientific evidence demonstrates that agro-ecological methods outperform the use of chemical fertilizers in boosting food production where the hungry live, especially in unfavourable environments (Schutter, 2011). The project will contribute to Uganda&#x2019;s vision 2040 of transforming Uganda from peasant and low income to a competitive mid income status &amp; National Development Plan III. The project will contribute to the national development agenda through increased adoption of agroecological practices, increased agricultural production and productivity, increased household income and improved livelihoods, and increased market access and competitiveness of agricultural products in domestic and improved environmental health.</narrative>
  </description>
